{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99603","id":2196423559,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6C6sOH","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99603","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99603.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99603.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99603","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99603/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99603/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99603/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/11dc4f2e5eb13e7a6c4f5269d709b1ca5f03b38d","number":99603,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Metal: Add MetalFX upscaling support","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Summary\r\n\r\nIntroduces support for MetalFX upscaling for macOS and iOS platforms. This expands the `rendering/scaling_3d/mode` property to allow specialisation for the macOS and iOS platforms:\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2024-12-08 at 08 35 07](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/94778bc3-5216-4329-a0e9-1ff9bf05a706)\r\n\r\n# Overview\r\n\r\nThese numbers are from a MacBook Pro M1 Max running macOS 15.2 beta.\r\n\r\n## Bistro Demo\r\n\r\nI'm capturing the Metal HUD logs, which includes present intervals and GPU times for each frame. I have written a couple of CLI tools to convert the Metal HUD logs into CSV, and to generate a SwiftUI chart from the CLI.\r\n\r\nAn example invocation:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nMTL_HUD_ENABLED=1 MTL_HUD_LOG_ENABLED=1 \\\r\n  Godot --rendering-driver metal --screen 1 --quit-after 1500 --disable-vsync \\\r\n  2>! ~/tmp/bistro-fsr2-mtlhud.txt\r\n```\r\n\r\n<figure>\r\n <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b9dcabf-40a4-4357-a24c-674e2cf5377b\" />\r\n <figcaption>FSR2, 20 seconds</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n\r\n<figure>\r\n <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b4a5996-911f-4c1a-b53c-8c9c24620037\" />\r\n <figcaption>MetalFX Temporal, 20 seconds</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n\r\nMetalFX is averaging about a 16% reduction in GPU time from around **39.7ms** down to **33.2ms**.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"ar